#!/usr/bin/env bash
# =============================================================================
# oc-t5-sweep — the five Duty T5 legs, one row per leg WITH the boundary applied
# =============================================================================
# WHY THIS EXISTS (T-11, 2026-11-20; triage.md §Continuous Relationship Linking)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Duty T5 asks five questions of every open `fix(`/`bug(`-titled issue, and until
# now every sweep re-derived all five BY HAND from gh, git and the ledger. That
# is the defect this tool removes: a hand count cannot be re-run, so a flag from
# last week is neither reproducible nor auditable, and the population boundaries
# — which are the whole reason the detector is usable rather than permanently
# red — lived only in a human's memory of which date to type.
#
# THE FIVE LEGS (canon: triage.md §Continuous Relationship Linking Mandate)
#   a  ORIGIN DECLARED   native parent exists, OR ANY comment's body matches one
#                        of `no parent derivable` / `root:` / `upstream-rooted` /
#                        `parent:` (or the issue BODY declares it — a lane that
#                        declares its root in the body is equally compliant).
#                        ALL comments, never the first: a declaration posted
#                        retroactively cannot be the first comment on an issue
#                        that already carries a commit or design note.
#   b  ASSIGNEE          the REST `assignees` set is non-empty. A real field on
#                        the issue object (unlike `.parent`, whose REST
#                        projection returns a confident null for EVERY issue).
#   c  NATIVE LINK       where the origin resolves to a SAME-TRACKER issue, a
#                        native parent must exist. A comment-only `root:` makes
#                        the issue DECLARED (leg a) and still leaves the LINK
#                        absent (leg c) — the two legs are not redundant.
#   i  VALIDATION NOTE   `duplicate` / `reproduc` / `still reproduces` in the
#                        FIRST comment body, OR ANY claim row for the issue, OR
#                        the issue body. The record is PER-ISSUE, never
#                        per-claim-row: re-claiming is routine, and a lane that
#                        validated once does not un-validate by re-claiming.
#   ii DESIGN COMMENT    a comment `createdAt` before the earliest fork-main
#                        commit whose `Issue-Ref` trailer names the issue, OR a
#                        claim row declaring the repair mechanical.
#
# BOUNDARIES ARE DECLARED, PRINTED AND OVERRIDABLE — never inherited silently
#   legs a, c   created >= 2026-09-25T22:33:06Z  (oc-issue-create began refusing
#                                                 a silent fix-title)
#   leg  b      created >= 2026-10-05T10:19:00Z  (the owner order that added it)
#   legs i, ii  claimed >= 2026-09-26T22:00:00Z  (the pre-design law landed)
# An issue filed or claimed before its gate was never asked, so flagging it
# measures history rather than compliance — that distinction is what makes the
# detector actionable (whole-open-set: 92.8% flagged, permanently red;
# post-gate: 16.1%). EVERY ROW NAMES THE BOUNDARY IT APPLIED, and a `--boundary`
# override is visible in the row as `boundary=... (override)`.
#
# THE VACUOUS CASE IS NAMED, because a leg that cannot go red must not read clean
#   leg c   reports VACUOUS when NO in-scope issue declares a same-tracker root:
#           the referent does not exist, so "0 flagged" is the ABSENCE OF THE
#           THING MEASURED, not a pass.
#   leg ii  a missing anchor is the ABSENCE OF THE THING MEASURED, never a
#           failure (triage.md, measured 2026-09-28): an issue with no fork-main
#           commit naming it is VACUOUS, NOT flagged. The opposite reading flags
#           20 issues on a condition none of them can satisfy.
#
# This tool REPORTS. It closes nothing and writes nothing to any tracker — a
# public close is `oc-closure-sweep`'s / `oc-smoke --close`'s job, on a
# behavioural receipt. A flag here is a question to the filing lane, never a
# verdict, and it is registered by the CRON'S DELIVERY LANE: the T5 executor is
# UNBOUND, so `oc-questions ask` refuses it rc=2 by construction.
#
# Usage: oc-t5-sweep [--repo <owner/repo>] [--boundary leg=<a|b|c|i|ii>:<ISO>]
#                    [--ledger <path>] [--repo-dir <git checkout>]
#                    [--fixture <snapshot.json>] [--leg <name>] [--json]
#                    [--selftest]
#   --repo      tracker to sweep (default leshchenko1979/opencrabs, the fork —
#               the single binary tracker; factory issues are NOT in scope)
#   --boundary  override a leg's default boundary; repeatable, e.g.
#               --boundary leg=a:2026-09-30T00:00:00Z. The override is PRINTED
#               in that leg's row, so a re-run never has to be trusted.
#   --ledger    workers-ledger.json (default $STATE_DIR/workers-ledger.json)
#   --repo-dir  git checkout whose origin/main carries the Issue-Ref trailers
#               (default /root/opencrabs)
#   --fixture   evaluate a PRE-FETCHED snapshot instead of calling gh/git. This
#               is the reproducibility path: the hand count was captured this
#               way, so the tool can be re-run offline against the same bytes.
#   --leg       restrict the run to one leg (a|b|c|i|ii), repeatable
#   --json      one JSON object per leg on stdout
#
# Exit codes:
#   0 sweep ran; no leg flagged a finding
#   1 sweep ran; at least one leg flagged (findings, not an error)
#   2 usage error
#   3 an input is missing or unreadable (--ledger / --fixture / gh unavailable)
# =============================================================================
# --- oc-snap guard: run from an immutable mirror (fork #167; tools/lib/oc-snap.sh)
# --- oc-root bootstrap: resolve the tools dir at ANY depth (tools/lib/oc-root.sh)
_oc_r="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" 2>/dev/null && pwd)" || _oc_r="."; _oc_d="$_oc_r"; while [ "$_oc_r" != "/" ] && [ "$_oc_r" != "." ] && ! { [ -f "$_oc_r/lib/oc-root.sh" ] && [ ! -L "$_oc_r/lib" ]; } && [ "$(basename "$_oc_r")" != "tools" ]; do _oc_r="$(dirname "$_oc_r")"; done
if [ "$(basename "$_oc_r")" = "tools" ]; then _oc_d="$_oc_r"; fi
if [ -f "$_oc_r/lib/oc-root.sh" ] && [ ! -L "$_oc_r/lib" ]; then . "$_oc_r/lib/oc-root.sh"; else OC_TOOLS_DIR="$(cd "$_oc_d" && pwd)"; fi
_OC_SNAP="$OC_TOOLS_DIR/lib/oc-snap.sh"
if [ -f "$_OC_SNAP" ]; then . "$_OC_SNAP"; oc_snap_guard "$0" "$@"; fi

set -u
set -o pipefail

PROG="oc-t5-sweep"
STATE_DIR="${OC_DEPLOY_STATE_DIR:-${OC_DEV_STATE:-$HOME/.opencrabs/profiles/ops/opencrabs-dev}}"

# The selftest must not journal rows into the fleet log. Set BEFORE oc_log_init:
# init is what enables the writer, so exporting after it is a no-op.
for _a in "$@"; do [ "$_a" = "--selftest" ] && export OC_TOOLS_NOLOG=1; done

. "$OC_TOOLS_DIR/lib/oc-log.sh" 2>/dev/null || true
oc_log_init "$PROG" "$@"

GH_BIN="${OC_GH_BIN:-gh}"
REPO="leshchenko1979/opencrabs"
LEDGER="$STATE_DIR/workers-ledger.json"
REPO_DIR="${OC_SRC_DIR:-/root/opencrabs}"
FIXTURE=""
JSON=0
MODE=sweep
ORIGIN_GATE="2026-09-25T22:33:06Z"   # legs a AND c
BOUND_A="$ORIGIN_GATE"
BOUND_B="2026-10-05T10:19:00Z"
BOUND_C="2026-09-26T22:00:00Z"        # legs i and ii (design gate)
BOUND_C_LEG="$ORIGIN_GATE"            # leg c, overridable on its own
OVR_A=""; OVR_B=""; OVR_C=""; OVR_I=""; OVR_II=""
LEGS="a b c i ii"
LEG_GIVEN=0

die() { local rc="$1"; shift; printf '%s: %s\n' "$PROG" "$*" >&2; exit "$rc"; }

usage() {
  sed -n '/^# Usage: oc-t5-sweep/,/^#   3 an input is missing/p' "$0" | sed 's/^# \{0,1\}//'
}

while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
  case "$1" in
    --repo)      [ $# -ge 2 ] || die 2 "--repo needs <owner/repo>"; REPO="$2"; shift 2 ;;
    --ledger)    [ $# -ge 2 ] || die 2 "--ledger needs a path"; LEDGER="$2"; shift 2 ;;
    --repo-dir)  [ $# -ge 2 ] || die 2 "--repo-dir needs a path"; REPO_DIR="$2"; shift 2 ;;
    --fixture)   [ $# -ge 2 ] || die 2 "--fixture needs a path"; FIXTURE="$2"; shift 2 ;;
    --leg)       [ $# -ge 2 ] || die 2 "--leg needs a name"
                 [ "$LEG_GIVEN" -eq 1 ] || { LEGS=""; LEG_GIVEN=1; }
                 LEGS="$LEGS $2"; shift 2 ;;
    --boundary)
      [ $# -ge 2 ] || die 2 "--boundary needs leg=<name>:<ISO>"
      case "$2" in
        leg=*) ;;
        *) die 2 "--boundary must be leg=<name>:<ISO>, got '$2'" ;;
      esac
      _bl="${2#leg=}"; _lg="${_bl%%:*}"; _iso="${_bl#*:}"
      case "$_lg" in
        a)  OVR_A="$_iso" ;;
        b)  OVR_B="$_iso" ;;
        c)  OVR_C="$_iso" ;;
        i)  OVR_I="$_iso" ;;
        ii) OVR_II="$_iso" ;;
        *) die 2 "--boundary leg name must be one of a|b|c|i|ii, got '$_lg'" ;;
      esac
      case "$_iso" in
        [0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]T[0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9]Z) ;;
        *) die 2 "--boundary instant must be RFC3339 UTC (YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ssZ), got '$_iso'" ;;
      esac
      shift 2 ;;
    --json)      JSON=1; shift ;;
    --selftest)  MODE=selftest; shift ;;
    -h|--help)   usage; exit 0 ;;
    *) die 2 "unknown argument '$1' (see --help)" ;;
  esac
done

case "$REPO" in
  */*) ;;
  *) die 2 "--repo must be owner/repo, got '$REPO'" ;;
esac

# Normalise the leg list: dedupe, validate, keep canonical order.
_norm=""
for _l in a b c i ii; do
  for _want in $LEGS; do
    [ "$_want" = "$_l" ] && { _norm="$_norm $_l"; break; }
  done
done
LEGS="${_norm# }"
[ -n "$LEGS" ] || die 2 "--leg names must be one of a|b|c|i|ii"

# Overrides replace the default for that leg. Empty means "use the default".
[ -n "$OVR_A" ]  && BOUND_A="$OVR_A"
[ -n "$OVR_B" ]  && BOUND_B="$OVR_B"
[ -n "$OVR_C" ]  && BOUND_C_LEG="$OVR_C"
# legs i and ii share the design-gate boundary; an override on either leg
# applies to THAT leg only, so the row can never claim a boundary it did not use.
BOUND_I="${OVR_I:-$BOUND_C}"
BOUND_II="${OVR_II:-$BOUND_C}"

export PROG REPO LEDGER REPO_DIR FIXTURE JSON LEGS GH_BIN
export BOUND_A BOUND_B BOUND_C BOUND_C_LEG BOUND_I BOUND_II OVR_A OVR_B OVR_C OVR_I OVR_II

# =============================================================================
# The sweep itself. ONE code path serves live and --fixture runs: live mode
# builds the same snapshot dict the fixture supplies, so the selftest exercises
# the evaluator that actually ships rather than a parallel copy of it.
# =============================================================================
sweep() {
python3 - <<'PY'
import json, os, re, subprocess, sys, collections

E = os.environ
REPO, FIXTURE = E["REPO"], E["FIXTURE"]
LEDGER, REPO_DIR = E["LEDGER"], E["REPO_DIR"]
GH = E["GH_BIN"]
LEGS = E["LEGS"].split()
AS_JSON = E["JSON"] == "1"
B = {"a": E["BOUND_A"], "b": E["BOUND_B"], "c": E["BOUND_C_LEG"],
     "i": E["BOUND_I"], "ii": E["BOUND_II"]}
OVR = {"a": E["OVR_A"], "b": E["OVR_B"], "c": E["OVR_C"],
       "i": E["OVR_I"], "ii": E["OVR_II"]}
SRC = {k: ("override" if OVR[k] else "default") for k in B}

FIXTITLE = re.compile(r'^(fix|bug)\(', re.I)
DECL = re.compile(r'no parent derivable|root:|upstream-rooted|parent:', re.I)
SAMEROOT = re.compile(r'root:\s*(?:#|https://github\.com/leshchenko1979/opencrabs/issues/)(\d+)', re.I)
VALID = re.compile(r'duplicate|reproduc|still reproduces', re.I)
MECH = re.compile(r'mechanical', re.I)


def die(rc, msg):
    sys.stderr.write("oc-t5-sweep: %s\n" % msg)
    sys.exit(rc)


def gh_json(args):
    # A MISSING gh is rc 3 (an input is unavailable), never a Python traceback:
    # a traceback reads as "the tool crashed", which sends the next reader
    # hunting a defect in the sweep instead of installing gh.
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([GH] + args, capture_output=True, text=True)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        die(3, "gh not found (%s) — install gh or set OC_GH_BIN" % GH)
    except OSError as exc:
        die(3, "gh could not be run (%s): %s" % (GH, exc))
    if r.returncode != 0:
        die(3, "gh %s: %s" % (" ".join(args[:2]), (r.stderr or "").strip()[:200]))
    return json.loads(r.stdout or "[]")


def load_live():
    """Build the snapshot: issues (with parent/comments), claims, anchors."""
    raw = gh_json(["issue", "list", "--repo", REPO, "--state", "open",
                   "--limit", "500", "--json", "number,title,createdAt,assignees"])
    issues = []
    for it in raw:
        if not FIXTITLE.search(it.get("title") or ""):
            continue
        issues.append({"number": it["number"], "title": it["title"],
                       "createdAt": it["createdAt"],
                       "assignees": [a.get("login") for a in (it.get("assignees") or [])]})
    # Detail is needed only where a leg reads parent/comments/body. Leg b reads
    # the list's own `assignees`, so an issue can be in its population with no
    # detail call at all.
    by_n = {i["number"]: i for i in issues}
    need = sorted({i["number"] for i in issues if i["createdAt"] >= min(B["a"], B["c"])})
    sys.stderr.write("oc-t5-sweep: reading %d issue(s) for parent/comments/body\n" % len(need))
    for n in need:
        d = gh_json(["issue", "view", str(n), "--repo", REPO,
                     "--json", "number,parent,assignees,body,comments"])
        by_n[n]["parent"] = (d.get("parent") or {}).get("number")
        by_n[n]["body"] = d.get("body") or ""
        by_n[n]["comments"] = [{"body": (c.get("body") or ""),
                                "createdAt": c.get("createdAt")}
                               for c in (d.get("comments") or [])]
    for i in issues:
        i.setdefault("parent", None); i.setdefault("body", ""); i.setdefault("comments", [])
    return {"issues": issues, "claims": load_claims(), "anchors": load_anchors()}


def load_claims():
    try:
        ev = json.load(open(LEDGER))["events"]
    except Exception as exc:
        die(3, "ledger unreadable (%s): %s" % (LEDGER, exc))
    return [{"n": e.get("n"), "t": e.get("t"), "what": e.get("what") or "",
             "issues": e.get("issues") or []}
            for e in ev if e.get("kind") == "claim"]


def load_anchors():
    """issue number -> earliest fork-main commit date whose Issue-Ref names it."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", REPO_DIR, "log", "origin/main",
                            "--format=%cI|%(trailers:key=Issue-Ref,valueonly)"],
                           capture_output=True, text=True)
    except Exception as exc:
        sys.stderr.write("oc-t5-sweep: anchors UNAVAILABLE (git: %s) — leg ii reports vacuous\n" % exc)
        return {}
    if r.returncode != 0:
        sys.stderr.write("oc-t5-sweep: anchors UNAVAILABLE (%s) — leg ii reports vacuous\n"
                         % (r.stderr or "").strip()[:160])
        return {}
    anchors = {}
    for line in r.stdout.splitlines():
        if "|" not in line:
            continue
        when, ref = line.split("|", 1)
        for m in re.finditer(r'#(\d+)', ref):
            n = int(m.group(1))
            if n not in anchors or when < anchors[n]:
                anchors[n] = when
    return anchors


def leg_a(issues, snap):
    pop = [i for i in issues if i["createdAt"] >= B["a"]]
    flagged = []
    for i in pop:
        if i.get("parent"):
            continue
        if any(DECL.search(c["body"]) for c in i["comments"]):
            continue
        if DECL.search(i["body"]):
            continue
        flagged.append(i["number"])
    return {"leg": "a", "predicate": "origin declared",
            "boundary_field": "created", "boundary": B["a"],
            "boundary_source": SRC["a"], "population": len(pop),
            "flagged": flagged, "vacuous": None}


def leg_b(issues, snap):
    pop = [i for i in issues if i["createdAt"] >= B["b"]]
    flagged = [i["number"] for i in pop if not i.get("assignees")]
    return {"leg": "b", "predicate": "assignee present",
            "boundary_field": "created", "boundary": B["b"],
            "boundary_source": SRC["b"], "population": len(pop),
            "flagged": flagged, "vacuous": None}


def leg_c(issues, snap):
    pop = [i for i in issues if i["createdAt"] >= B["c"]]
    flagged, with_root = [], 0
    for i in pop:
        roots = set()
        for c in i["comments"]:
            for m in SAMEROOT.finditer(c["body"]):
                roots.add(int(m.group(1)))
        if roots:
            with_root += 1
            if not i.get("parent"):
                flagged.append(i["number"])
    vac = None
    if with_root == 0:
        # NOT a pass: the referent does not exist, so nothing was measured.
        vac = {"count": len(pop),
               "reason": "no in-scope issue declares a same-tracker root"}
    return {"leg": "c", "predicate": "native link where origin resolves same-tracker",
            "boundary_field": "created", "boundary": B["c"],
            "boundary_source": SRC["c"], "population": len(pop),
            "flagged": flagged, "vacuous": vac, "with_same_tracker_root": with_root}


def _claimed(snap, issues, bound):
    popn = {i["number"]: i for i in issues}
    claims = collections.defaultdict(list)
    for c in snap["claims"]:
        for n in c["issues"]:
            try:
                claims[int(n)].append(c)
            except (TypeError, ValueError):
                pass
    scope = sorted(n for n, cs in claims.items()
                   if n in popn and any((c["t"] or "") >= bound for c in cs))
    return scope, claims, popn


def leg_i(issues, snap):
    scope, claims, popn = _claimed(snap, issues, B["i"])
    flagged = []
    for n in scope:
        i = popn[n]
        first = i["comments"][0]["body"] if i["comments"] else ""
        ok = (VALID.search(first)
              or any(VALID.search(c["what"]) for c in claims[n])
              or VALID.search(i["body"]))
        if not ok:
            flagged.append(n)
    return {"leg": "i", "predicate": "validation note on the record",
            "boundary_field": "claimed", "boundary": B["i"],
            "boundary_source": SRC["i"], "population": len(scope),
            "flagged": flagged, "vacuous": None}


def leg_ii(issues, snap):
    scope, claims, popn = _claimed(snap, issues, B["ii"])
    anchors = snap["anchors"]
    flagged, vacuous = [], 0
    for n in scope:
        i = popn[n]
        anchor = anchors.get(n) or anchors.get(str(n))
        mech = any(MECH.search(c["what"]) for c in claims[n])
        if anchor is None:
            # ABSENCE OF THE THING MEASURED, never a failure (triage.md).
            vacuous += 1
            continue
        ok = mech or any((c["createdAt"] or "") and c["createdAt"] < anchor
                         for c in i["comments"])
        if not ok:
            flagged.append(n)
    vac = None
    if vacuous:
        vac = {"count": vacuous,
               "reason": "no fork-main commit carries an Issue-Ref for these issues"}
    return {"leg": "ii", "predicate": "design comment precedes first anchored commit",
            "boundary_field": "claimed", "boundary": B["ii"],
            "boundary_source": SRC["ii"], "population": len(scope),
            "flagged": flagged, "vacuous": vac}


if FIXTURE:
    try:
        snap = json.load(open(FIXTURE))
    except Exception as exc:
        die(3, "fixture unreadable (%s): %s" % (FIXTURE, exc))
    for k in ("issues", "claims", "anchors"):
        snap.setdefault(k, [] if k != "anchors" else {})
    snap["anchors"] = {int(k): v for k, v in (snap["anchors"] or {}).items()}
else:
    snap = load_live()

issues = snap["issues"]
rows = []
for lg in LEGS:
    rows.append({"a": leg_a, "b": leg_b, "c": leg_c, "i": leg_i, "ii": leg_ii}[lg](issues, snap))

total = 0
for r in rows:
    total += len(r["flagged"])
    if AS_JSON:
        print(json.dumps(r, sort_keys=True))
        continue
    src = " (override)" if r["boundary_source"] == "override" else ""
    line = ("leg %-2s %-46s boundary=%s>=%s%s  population=%d  flagged=%d"
            % (r["leg"], r["predicate"], r["boundary_field"], r["boundary"], src,
               r["population"], len(r["flagged"])))
    if r["flagged"]:
        line += "\n       flags: " + " ".join("#%d" % n for n in r["flagged"])
    if r.get("vacuous"):
        line += "\n       VACUOUS (%s) — %d issue(s) not measured; NOT a pass" % (
            r["vacuous"]["reason"], r["vacuous"]["count"])
    print(line)

if not AS_JSON:
    print("\ntotal flagged across legs: %d" % total)
    print("boundaries: a created>=%s  b created>=%s  c created>=%s  i claimed>=%s  ii claimed>=%s"
          % (B["a"], B["b"], B["c"], B["i"], B["ii"]))

sys.exit(1 if total else 0)
PY
}

# =============================================================================
# SELFTEST — fixtures only; never touches gh, git or the live ledger.
# A leg that cannot go red is decoration, so each arm below FAILS if the
# predicate it targets is neutered.
# =============================================================================
run_selftest() {
  export OC_TOOLS_NOLOG=1
  _ST_D="$(mktemp -d)" || die 3 "mktemp failed"
  trap 'rm -rf "$_ST_D"' EXIT
  D="$_ST_D"
  local SELF="$OC_TOOLS_DIR/state/oc-t5-sweep"
  local pass=0 fail=0
  # ONE label per arm, printed by BOTH outcomes. A t_bad that words the failure
  # differently from its t_ok makes the arm unsearchable in a mutation run —
  # measured here: two neutered predicates read as "SURVIVED" because the
  # harness matched the OK string and the FAIL string said something else.
  t_ok()  { pass=$((pass + 1)); printf 'selftest: %s  OK\n' "$*"; }
  t_bad() { fail=$((fail + 1)); printf 'selftest: %s  FAIL\n' "$*" >&2; }
  ck() { local l="$1"; shift; if "$@"; then t_ok "$l"; else t_bad "$l"; fi; }
  # rows-based assertion: a python expression over `rows` exits 0/1
  chk() {
    local l="$1" expr="$2"
    python3 -c "
import json,sys
rows=[json.loads(x) for x in open('$D/out.json') if x.strip()]
$expr
" 2>/dev/null && t_ok "$l" || t_bad "$l"
  }

  # ---- fixture: every leg has a pass arm and a red arm ---------------------
  # #7 is created BEFORE leg a/c's boundary and claimed BEFORE the design gate:
  # it must be OUT of both populations, which is the boundary arm.
  # #3 carries an ANCHOR on purpose. Without one it goes vacuous before the
  # mechanical arm is ever read, so removing `mech or` survived every leg.
  cat > "$D/f.json" <<'FIX'
{"issues":[
 {"number":1,"createdAt":"2026-10-10T00:00:00Z","parent":9,"assignees":["x"],"body":"","comments":[]},
 {"number":2,"createdAt":"2026-10-10T00:00:00Z","parent":null,"assignees":[],"body":"",
  "comments":[{"body":"unrelated note","createdAt":"2026-10-11T00:00:00Z"},
              {"body":"root: upstream:abc123","createdAt":"2026-10-12T00:00:00Z"}]},
 {"number":3,"createdAt":"2026-10-10T00:00:00Z","parent":null,"assignees":[],
  "body":"root: upstream:deadbeef","comments":[]},
 {"number":4,"createdAt":"2026-10-10T00:00:00Z","parent":null,"assignees":["x"],"body":"","comments":[]},
 {"number":5,"createdAt":"2026-10-10T00:00:00Z","parent":null,"assignees":["x"],"body":"",
  "comments":[{"body":"root: #9","createdAt":"2026-09-28T00:00:00Z"}]},
 {"number":6,"createdAt":"2026-10-10T00:00:00Z","parent":9,"assignees":["x"],"body":"",
